Recursive Compounding

Core Law

A new contribution does more than add value.

It can reinterpret the accumulated structure, increase the value of earlier contributions, and alter the basis from which future growth begins.

K_{t+1}
=
\mathcal{C}(K_t,x_t)

where

\mathcal{C}(K,x)
=
\operatorname{Reenter}
\left(
\operatorname{Propagate}
\left(
\operatorname{Reframe}
\left(
\operatorname{Connect}
\left(
\operatorname{Accumulate}(K,x)
\right)
\right)
\right)
\right)

Five Primitive Operators

\boxed{
A \rightarrow C \rightarrow R \rightarrow P \rightarrow E
}

Accumulate
Preserve the new contribution and the prior state.

Connect
Discover relationships between the contribution and the existing corpus.

Reframe
Change the coordinate system through which earlier material is interpreted.

Propagate
Carry the consequences of that reinterpretation through the network.

Reenter
Use the transformed whole as the starting state of the next cycle.

Minimal Equation

\boxed{
K_{t+1}
=
K_t
+
x_t
+
\Delta_{\text{relations}}
+
\Delta_{\text{reinterpretation}}
+
\Delta_{\text{future capacity}}
}

The value of an addition is therefore:

V(x_t\mid K_t)
=
V_{\text{direct}}
+
V_{\text{unlocked past}}
+
V_{\text{new relations}}
+
V_{\text{future options}}

Base Meaning

Add to the whole.
Let the addition alter the whole.
Compound from the altered whole.

Atomic Token

