The pressure does not supply all the energy.

It directs energy already accumulated in the system.

Graph Translation

Let:

G_t=(N_t,E_t,\Phi_t)

where:

* N_t contains concepts,
* E_t contains relationships,
* \Phi_t contains interpretive frames.

A new contribution may:

x_t:
\begin{cases}
\text{add a node}\\
\text{add an edge}\\
\text{create a higher-order cluster}\\
\text{change the frame applied to the graph}
\end{cases}

The highest-leverage contribution is often not another node.

It is a frame that makes many existing nodes newly legible.

Compiler Form

def recursive_compound(corpus, addition):
    corpus = accumulate(corpus, addition)
    candidates = retrieve_related(
        corpus=corpus,
        query=addition,
    )
    relations = connect(
        addition=addition,
        candidates=candidates,
    )
    reframed = reinterpret(
        corpus=corpus,
        relations=relations,
        preserve_prior_frames=True,
    )
    propagated = propagate(
        corpus=reframed,
        changed_relations=relations,
    )
    return reenter(propagated)

