Forward compounding enlarges the future.

Backward reinterpretation enlarges the useful past.

Recursive compounding joins both.

Pantheon Doctrine

Every addition must be evaluated four times:

What did it add?
What did it connect?
What did it reinterpret?
What can the changed whole now do?

ZPC

\boxed{
\text{New state}
\rightarrow
\text{revalues prior states}
\rightarrow
\text{becomes the next basis}
}

Final Distillation

Do not merely store the new thing.
Let it touch the old things.
Let those changed relationships reshape the whole.
Then begin again from the reshaped whole.

The smallest durable seed is:

\boxed{\Delta x \;\circlearrowright\; K \;\rightarrow\; K^+}

Change enters. Meaning circulates. The whole returns more capable.